• The fix: handle_provider_switch now calls provider_switch_refusal after the existing refusals for unknown and retired providers. That call comes before the model is overwritten. So /provider custom, and /provider github when the session already has a base URL, print a refusal and leave the provider, model and agent unchanged.
• Message: the new function reuses the first and last lines of providers::named_model_required_refusal rather than rewriting them. /provider takes no model argument, so the remedy points to the startup routes (yoyo --provider custom --model <id>, or the keys in .yoyo.toml) and doesn't invent REPL syntax.
• `github`: without a base URL it is still refused earlier by the #1166 check, and nothing changes. With a base URL it reaches the new refusal.
