  • The full refusal text for custom is checked both with and without a base URL.
  • Providers that don't need a named model (such as openai) still switch and get their default.
  • The remedy command is split by a real shell and fed back through parse_args_with_config, and the provider, model and base URL land where intended.
• Nothing left dangling: the new function is used by the handler and the tests. The test file is wired in through #[path], and no enums or names changed. The only #1183 references left are code and test comments, none of them user-facing.
